1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,650
You have a presentation

2
00:00:00,680 --> 00:00:02,300
that could change your career.

3
00:00:02,680 --> 00:00:03,480
So naturally,

4
00:00:03,620 --> 00:00:04,690
this is the perfect moment

5
00:00:04,720 --> 00:00:06,240
to clean your kitchen.

6
00:00:06,880 --> 00:00:07,720
Not the whole kitchen.

7
00:00:08,060 --> 00:00:09,550
Just enough to feel productive

8
00:00:09,580 --> 00:00:11,620
while the presentation sits unopened.

9
00:00:12,280 --> 00:00:13,560
Then you answer a message.

10
00:00:14,220 --> 00:00:15,260
Check tomorrow’s weather.

11
00:00:15,920 --> 00:00:17,860
Research a better note-taking app.

12
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:18,570
Somehow,

13
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:20,490
the task you care about most

14
00:00:20,520 --> 00:00:22,620
becomes the one thing you cannot touch.

15
00:00:22,840 --> 00:00:24,130
If that feels familiar,

16
00:00:24,160 --> 00:00:25,600
the useful question isn’t,

17
00:00:25,780 --> 00:00:26,670
“Why am I so lazy?”

18
00:00:26,700 --> 00:00:27,880
It’s,

19
00:00:28,060 --> 00:00:29,170
“What happens when I get close

20
00:00:29,200 --> 00:00:30,860
to this particular task?”
